{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS4y6heUpwJi5tbkP16f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the generator so it sends each heart-rate (HR) range in a form Intervals reads as a range. It hasn't been tested on the watch yet, because nothing was pushed.\n\n**Cause:** `gen.py` sent each range as `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}`. In Intervals' workout format, `value` is a single target and a range is written as `start` + `end`. Our mix of the two was stored without complaint but never became a range. The watch notes back this up: every band shown is the watch zone that contains the step's upper limit:\n\n| step | upper limit | watch showed |\n|---|---|---|\n| Warm-up | 129 | Z2 |\n| Tempo | 160 | Z4 |\n| Float | 141 | Z3 |\n| Cool-down | 124 | Z2 |\n\nSo the lower limit was dropped and the watch got a zone target instead of a custom bpm range. That's also why changing the watch's LTHR only moved the bands.\n\n**Fix (`gen.py`, `hr_target`):** ranges are now sent as `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}`. A step with equal low and high is sent as a single `value`. Targets stay in % of LTHR, so Intervals still converts them to bpm using LTHR 172. I didn't bring back the earlier `bpm` or `start_bpm`/`end_bpm` tries from the notes, since those produced 214–249 and a constant 101.\n\nTo check it, push the event (`python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json > event.json && ./push.sh event.json`) and sync the watch. Tempo should show 151–160 and Float 129–141. The full explanation is in `ANSWER.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1118,"cache_read_input_tokens":24593,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1118},"output_tokens":570,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnosti